The Mission of Department of REMOTE SENSING AND GIS (RSG-SRTI-BAS) is "Development, improvement, and transfer of methods for environmental studies with integrated use of Earth observation technologies, geoinformation systems and ground-based methods. Education of Master students, PhD students, and specialists in the field".
The Department comprises 14 researchers and specialists (as of 2021): a Professor, two Associate Professors,six Assistants Professors (of then,three Doctors and three extramural PhD students*), two Assistants &ndash;extramural PhD students*, three specialists with higher education (of then, two extramural PhD students). They have various qualifications &ndash; geographers, landscape ecologists, engineers, a geologist, and an archeologist.

In the Department there are two separate research laboratories and a research complex:
1. SPACEBIOLAB - SPACE BIOTECHNOLOGY LABORATORY Person responsible - Assist. Prof. Iliana Ilieva, MS;
2. FLSSM - FIELD LABORATORY FOR SUB-SATELLITE MEASUREMENTS Person responsible - Prof. Georgi Jelev, PhD;
The main activities of the RSG-SRTI-BAS Department are in:
&Oslash; Development of the Scientific-Research Complex(SRC) of Bulgarian Aerospace Test Sites (BASTSs);
&Oslash; Transfer of remote sensing of the Earth technologies into the field of landscape-ecologicalassessment of the environment,tourism, and cultural and historical heritage;
&Oslash; Assessment of agricultural crop development using vegetation satellite productswith spatial resolution of250&ndash;300m;
&Oslash; Geoecological study of hazardous natural processesand integrated risk assessment for the needs ofregional management;

&Oslash; Providing consultation and training of PhD students in the field of higher education "4. Natural Sciences, Mathematics and Informatics", Professional field "4.4 Earth Sciences", Scientific speciality "Remote Sensing of the Earth and Planets" which is among the subjects of accreditation of the SRTI&ndash;BAS.

The Italian Rowing Federation, "F.I.C.", founded in Turin in 1888 under the name of Italian Rowing Club later, is a non-profit association with legal personality under private law pursuant to art. 18 of Law Decree 242 of July 23, 1999 and subsequent amendments and additions to the recognized sporting purposes by the National Council of CONI (Italian National Olympic Committee). Its headquarters are located in Rome. 
F.I.C. is formed and empowered by the rowing clubs and/or multisport associations properly equipped, with the prescribed requirements and regularly subsidiaries, hereinafter referred to as subject "affiliates", which are currently over 210.
The Italian -Rowing Federation is an organization leaded by a President and a Board of Directors composed by ten members elected by the National Congress, composed by the legal representative of affiliated clubs and associations. 
The goals and objectives of F.I.C. are to efficiently DEVELOP, PROMOTE, PRESENT and GOVERN the sport of rowing and para-rowing
F.I.C.&rsquo;s vision is to encourage the development of the sport of rowing and para-rowing and strengthen the bonds that unite those who practice it. 
F.I.C. has the purpose of:
a) organize, regulate, disseminate, promote, develop and carry through affiliates, in Italy and on the international context, the sport of rowing at the amateur level in all its forms - Olympic and non, on all kinds of boats including "Coastal Rowing ", and preparatory activities such as indoor rowing machines and rowing simulators including the implementation of the training programs of athletes, coaches and umpires;
b) organize, disseminate, promote, develop and carry through affiliates, nationally and internationally, the '"Para-rowing" in accordance with the rules and regulations of the International Paralympic Committee;
c) participate in international competitions;
d) coordinate the activities of Affiliates, protecting their interests with the Local Authorities, National Federations of other counties as well as at any other entity concerned;
e) provide the resources to resolve disputes between members and affiliated parties relating to rowing;
f) organize and regulate, either directly or through organizing committees the conduct of national and international competitions, approving results, within the guidelines issued by the CONI and International Federations and in accordance with the principles contained in the Olympic Charter.
F.I.C. also carries out the following activities, and issue directives regarding:
affiliate societies and sports clubs;
the establishment of the local organizing committees for national and international events;
checks on clubs and sports associations;
membership;
protection of the health insurance and registered athletes;
prevention and combating doping unconditionally accepting the CONI Anti-Doping Rules sports;
training of managers, the coaches and umpires.
To achieve its institutional aims and purposes, FIC may perform any operation including financial security, which is the real estate in respect of the absence of profit motive.

